  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently when looking at active worlds, the user count reflects all public instances of that world. This means that any instance that calls back to the API (this includes friends+ and friends only) are reflected in the user count. However, you can only join on public instances of these worlds, so why doesn't the user count accurately reflect that? You can go to any 50+ user world in the active worlds list, and you'll only receive instances with 2 or 3 users amounting to only a fraction of what the active world list tells you.",
